      "text": "The given expression is a variation of the arithmetic series where the terms alternate between subtracting and adding. The sequence starts at 1 and increases by 3 each time until it reaches 49, then continues with an odd number until 55.\n\nTo solve the expression, we can separate it into two parts:\n- The sum of the series when it's subtracted: \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49\\)\n- The sum of the series when it's added: \\(13 - 16 + 19 - 22 + 25 - \\cdots - 52 + 55\\)\n\nFirst, let's look at the first part of the series \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49\\). This series is an arithmetic series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and a common difference \\(d = 3\\). The number of terms in this series can be found by solving for \\(n\\) in the equation \\(1 + (n-1) \\cdot 3 = 49\\):\n\\[1 + 3(n-1) = 49\\]\n\\[3(n-1) = 48\\]\n\\[n-1 = 16\\]\n\\[n = 17\\]\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by the formula:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d)\\]\nFor our series, \\(a = 1\\), \\(d = 3\\), and \\(n = 17\\):\n\\[S_{17} = \\frac{17}{2} (2 \\cdot 1 + (17-1) \\cdot 3) = \\frac{17}{2} (2 + 16 \\cdot 3) = \\frac{17}{2} (2 + 48) = \\frac{17}{2} \\cdot 50 = 17 \\cdot 25 = 425\\]\n\nNext, let's look at the second part of the series \\(13 - 16 + 19 - 22 + 25 - \\cdots - 52 + 55\\). This series is also an arithmetic series with the first term \\(a = 13\\) and a common difference \\(d = 3\\). The number of terms in this series can be found by solving for \\(n\\) in the equation \\(13 + (n-1) \\cdot 3 = 55\\):\n\\[13 + 3(n-1) = 55\\]\n\\[3(n-1) = 42\\]\n\\[n-1 = 14\\]\n\\[n = 15\\]\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of this series is given by the formula:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (2a + (n-1)d)\\]\nFor our series, \\(a = 13\\), \\(d = 3\\), and \\(n = 15\\):\n\\[S_{15} = \\frac{15}{2} (2 \\cdot 13 + (15-1) \\cdot 3) = \\frac{15}{2} (26 + 14 \\cdot 3) = \\frac{15}{2} (26 + 42) = \\frac{15}{2} \\cdot 68 = 15 \\cdot 34 = 510\\]\n\nFinally, we combine the two sums:\n\\[425 + 510 = 935\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{935}\\).",
